course: dictionary
lesson: 7891
title: Ranking: putting things in order
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ranking is a position in a list that shows how good or important something is compared with others. «A world ranking of 5» means the player is fifth in the whole world.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The tennis rankings» is about a list, so rankings means the list itself. «Ranking order» is about how things are arranged from first to last.
explain: Ranking can also be a verb. In «Ranking your favourite foods is fun», it means putting the foods in order, from your favourite to your least favourite. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Ranking means putting things in order, such as 1st, 2nd and 3rd.
fact: A ranking is a position in a list that shows how good or important someone or something is.
fact: The rankings are the whole list, such as «the school league rankings».
fact: «World ranking» means a position compared with everyone in the world.
fact: Ranking is also a verb: you rank things, they ranked, you are ranking them.
exercise: «A world ranking of 5» means what? | A way of shouting very loudly | A kind of race that goes around in circles | A very large, round ball | *A position in a list, fifth in the world
exercise: «Ranking your favourite foods is fun.» What is ranking in this sentence? | Cooking a meal for friends | *Putting things in order | Eating things quickly | Counting the money
exercise: Which word means the whole list, as in «the tennis rankings»? | Champion | Tennis | Fastest | *Rankings
test: In the phrase «ranking order», what is being shown? | Things that are broken | *Things arranged from first to last | Things that are the same colour | Things that are hidden
test: A player with a «top ranking» is someone who is what? | *Among the highest in their list | Someone who is always late | Someone who does not play | Someone who has just started
exam: «The school league rankings show which schools are best.» What does ranking mean here? | Counting the children in each class | Building a new school | Painting the walls | *Putting schools in order by how good they are
